BT /F2 11 Tf 50.0 636.0 Td (1. Stacks, Queues & Recursion Viva Questions) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 619.0 Td (- Q1: What is the main disadvantage of a linear queue implemented via an array?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 603.0 Td (  A: False overflow condition occurs when elements are dequeued from front, leaving) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 589.0 Td (  unused space.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 573.0 Td (- Q2: How does a circular queue overcome false overflow?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 557.0 Td (  A: By wrapping rear and front pointers using modulo arithmetic: rear = \(rear + 1\) %) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 543.0 Td (  MAX.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 527.0 Td (- Q3: How does the system call stack facilitate recursion?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 511.0 Td (  A: Each recursive invocation allocates an activation record containing local variables) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 497.0 Td (  and return address.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 50.0 473.0 Td (2. Trees, Graphs & Complexity Viva Questions) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 456.0 Td (- Q4: What is the worst-case search complexity in an unbalanced BST vs an AVL tree?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 440.0 Td (  A: Unbalanced BST is O\(n\) \(skewed tree\); AVL tree maintains balance factor {-1,0,1}) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 426.0 Td (  guaranteeing O\(log n\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 410.0 Td (- Q5: Why is Quick Sort preferred over Merge Sort for arrays, and vice-versa for linked) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 396.0 Td (  lists?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 380.0 Td (  A: Quick Sort has superior cache locality and in-place partitioning; Merge Sort does) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 55.0 366.0 Td (  not require random access.) Tj ET
